+\begin{proof}
+Subtract an inner derivation to make $D(\omega)=0$.
+The map
+\[
+ L_{n+1}^{\,2}\longrightarrow L_{n+2},\qquad
+ (u,v)\longmapsto[u,b]+[a,v]
+\]
+is onto. The only inner derivation still preserving
+$\omega$ comes from its centralizer $\Q\omega$,
+so exactly one dimension is removed in degree two.
+The centralizer assertion follows from the leading
+word argument in the free associative algebra
+(or from the centralizer of a nonpower free Lie
+element). The involution acts as $(-1)^n$.
+
+The literature reduction is
+\citet[Theorem 10.7, Proposition 20.1,
+Corollary 20.2, Theorem 22.3, Corollary 23.3]{HainMatsumoto2020}.
+These identify the relative-completion monodromy
+image and its generators. Their ordinary $W$-degree
