+\begin{statement}{B.19}{Refuted}{The epsilon algebra is not the normalizer quotient}
+At type $(1,1)$ the proposed identification of the
+normalizer \emph{modulo geometry} with the algebra
+generated by the $\epsilon_{2k}$ is false. In the
+range of B.18 the corrected quotient is the odd
+mixed-Tate Lie algebra with degrees doubled.
+\end{statement}
+\begin{proof}
+The nonzero three-dimensional $\SL_2$-orbit of
+$\epsilon_4$ is geometric and is zero in the
+quotient. The quotient itself is zero in degree
+four, and has its first nonzero class in degree six.
+This is already a dimension counterexample.
+Through ordinary degree twelve its two lines
+are $\sigma_3,\sigma_5$ in degrees six and ten.
+Their brackets cannot produce a new class in the
+stated range: the self-bracket in degree twelve is
